Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 11:23:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11057/11362] Record that REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-4 is live and
 untested in production

The spec marks it Implemented with six mutation-proven tests, so a reader would
reasonably take it as proven. The one capstone since it shipped does not test it.

V611's capstone survived writing verdict_class null, but V611 was not
cascade-blocked -- it had a genuine null result and null was the correct class
whether or not the prompt said anything. The partial-versus-blocked decision the
fix exists for never arose.

The real test is the next capstone over a milestone whose upstreams were retired
or gate-blocked: does it declare blocked and get accepted on first write, or
declare partial and burn three attempts as v605 and v608 did.

Written after declining to write it an hour ago on the grounds that "nothing
happened, cause unclear" is noise. That reasoning was wrong for the same reason
the arc-news-watch note was right: a verification run that finishes inside the
old budget proves nothing about the new one, and a fix whose test case has not
occurred is an open question wearing a closed requirement's clothes.

